  "version": 1,
  "description": "Multilingual HR vocabulary used by collector/classify.py (title classification) and collector/public_sources.py (public job-bank search queries). Terms are written naturally; accents and case are normalised at load time exactly like job titles. A trailing * matches any word ending (German/Nordic compounds, Slavic inflections). Spaces also match hyphens, slashes and ampersands. 'strong' terms make a title HR on their own. 'contextual' terms count only when the title, or the same sentence of the text (application instructions excluded), also contains an hr_context term or a strong hr-generalist term, and the title has no non_hr_domain word. Every change must keep scripts/evaluate.py at zero errors; add positive and negative examples to data/evaluation.json.",
